# Store every text file with LF and check it out with LF on all platforms.
#
# Why this is pinned rather than left to each machine: .prettierrc.json sets
# endOfLine: "lf", so on a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true the checkout
# rewrites every file to CRLF and `pnpm format:check` then fails on the whole
# tree — while CI (ubuntu-latest, LF) stays green. The failure looks like a
# formatting problem and isn't one, and `prettier --write` "fixes" it by
# committing CRLF into the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never apply line-ending conversion.
*.png binary
